# OpenEVV sound map: Russian (eSpeak NG voice zle/ru), spoken by openevv's German module
# with the sounds, the melody and the tones of the language itself.
# Written by engine/accent/mapwriter.py; OpenEvvFrontend reads it, and docs/LANGUAGES.md
# says what each line means. Edit freely: the file is read each time a voice starts.

template dedx
style standard
vowels i I e E a A u U o O y Y oe OE @ aj aw oj a~ E~ o~ oe~ E: R
glides r l j w
schwa @
secondary 2

# the melody: late; a question that wants yes or no: risefall
accent f0=own range=108 shape=2 accent=34 accent2=14 unstressed=-6 decl=8 declmax=30 fs=-18 fw=-12 fc=14 fe=-12 fq=41 qreg=8 span=2 qfall=50 stop=1

# the words a question is asked with, which is not the question that wants yes or no
whwords first кто что где когда как почему зачем какой
whwords first какая какое какие сколько куда откуда чей чья
whwords first чьё чьи кого чего кому чему кем чем

# what the module says in place of a phone it is given
says C t S
says J d Z
says P p f
says T t s

